From d13fe6087e6cd4772c000878da23838dfaf42a65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arnaldo Lima <arnaldolimaof@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:43:18 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] cellVdec Ex, movie timing, perf overlay, job-module lifts;
 diagnostics

from gow-ascension-pc@676eefe

The opening cinematic plays (God of War: Ascension's OPENINGINT6.M2V):
- cellVdecQueryAttrEx / cellVdecOpenEx: unregistered, they faked CELL_OK
  without writing anything; the title got cmdDepth 0 and no handle and sat
  behind its black fade card.
- Pictures from an AU without a timestamp get pts/dts numbered one frame
  period apart, as the PS3 decoder (and RPCS3) does.
- CellVdecMpeg2Info carries frame_rate_code, aspect, progressive and picture
  structure: the title's player times its movie clock by frame_rate_code, and
  with 0 it never asked for a second picture.
- cellSpursJoinTask2 waits for the task's bit in the taskset to clear.

Performance:
- LD_PERF_OVERLAY=1: FPS, frame time, speed, CPU and GPU (PDH 3D engine) in
  the top-right corner, drawn on the CPU and copied into the backbuffer.
- Per-frame log lines (task creation/join, SPU dispatch, taskset starts,
  DecodeAu) follow PS3_VERBOSE.
- lift_jobmods.py --extra-funcs-json: per-module extra entries (every
  module shares LS 0x4000, so a global list splits other modules).

Diagnostics: LD_ZPROBE (one frame of a zeta: depth/stencil state, CPU
winding and z, depth readback), LD_DEPTH_EQUAL_LEQUAL, HLE_BT_NID (guest
stack of the first calls to one import), each distinct SPU interpreter
entry logged once with its start PC and resident overlay, GetPicture /
GetPicItem logs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
